[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     91[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Build configuration baked into the translation
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     92[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The C library is compiled with exactly:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     93[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT=5`, `XXH_NAMESPACE=ZSTD_`, `DYNAMIC_BMI2=0`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     94[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and *without* `ZSTD_MULTITHREAD`. Therefore:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     95[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `DYNAMIC_BMI2` is 0  -> there is only ONE version of every `*_bmi2` /
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     96[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `*_default` template pair; `ZSTD_cpuSupportsBmi2()` returns 0; `bmi2` flags
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     97[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   are threaded through but never change behaviour. Translate the non-BMI2 body.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     98[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `ZSTD_MULTITHREAD` undefined -> `ZSTD_pthread_*` are no-ops, `POOL_add` runs
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     99[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the job synchronously on the calling thread, `ZSTDMT_createCCtx_advanced`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    100[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   returns NULL, `nbWorkers` is forced to 0.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    101[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT=5` -> in `legacy/zstd_legacy.h` only v05, v06, v07 are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    102[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   reachable from the dispatcher, BUT zstd_v01.c..zstd_v04.c still compile their
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    103[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   full bodies and still export their symbols. Translate all of v01..v07.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    104[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `DEBUGLEVEL` is 0 -> `assert()`, `DEBUGLOG`, `RAWLOG`, `ZSTD_STATIC_ASSERT`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    105[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `DEBUG_STATIC_ASSERT` all compile to nothing. Drop them. Never translate an
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    106[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `assert` into a Rust `assert!`/`debug_assert!` (a panic would change behaviour).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    107[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    108[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Rust style rules (MANDATORY)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    109[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. Public C entry points:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    110[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    ```rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    111[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    #[unsafe(no_mangle)]
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    112[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    pub unsafe extern "C" fn ZSTD_foo(dst: *mut c_void, dstCapacity: size_t) -> size_t { ... }
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    113[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    114[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    The `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` name MUST equal the final linker symbol. Watch for
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    115[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    header macros that rename functions (e.g. xxhash's `XXH_NAMESPACE=ZSTD_`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    116[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    makes `XXH32` link as `ZSTD_XXH32`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    117[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `static` C functions become plain (non-`no_mangle`) `pub unsafe fn`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    118[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. Use raw pointers (`*const u8`, `*mut u8`, `*mut c_void`, ...) and `unsafe`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    119[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    freely. Fidelity beats safety here. Cast with `as`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    120[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 3. Integer arithmetic: C's unsigned arithmetic wraps. Use `wrapping_add`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    121[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `wrapping_sub`, `wrapping_mul`, `wrapping_neg` wherever the C value could
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    122[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    overflow or go "negative" in an unsigned type. The crate is built with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    123[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `overflow-checks = false`, but be explicit anyway on any expression that can
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    124[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    wrap. Pointer difference: `(a as isize) - (b as isize)` or
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    125[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `a.offset_from(b)`. Pointer +/- possibly-negative amounts: use `.offset(i)`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    126[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    with an `isize`, or `.wrapping_add`/`.wrapping_sub` with a `usize`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    127[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 4. C `enum`s become `pub type Foo = c_uint;` plus `pub const` variants (already
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    128[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    the pattern in the foundation files). Never a Rust `enum`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    129[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 5. `struct`s that cross the ABI, or that are memcpy'd / placed in workspaces,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    130[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    MUST be `#[repr(C)]`. When in doubt use `#[repr(C)]`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    131[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 6. C `switch` with fallthrough must be translated so the fallthrough still
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    132[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    happens (chain of `if`s, or duplicate the code). Do not silently drop it.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    133[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 7. File-scope `static` mutable C globals become
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    134[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `static mut NAME: T = ...;` accessed via `&raw mut NAME` / `&raw const NAME`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    135[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    Read-only tables become `static NAME: [T; N] = [...];`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    136[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 8. Keep C names verbatim (including camelCase). The crate already has
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    137[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `#![allow(non_snake_case)]` etc. at the top of lib.rs.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    138[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 9. Do NOT use `panic!`, `unwrap`, `expect`, `assert!`, slice indexing on raw
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    139[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    memory, or anything else that can panic on malformed input. Index raw memory
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    140[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    through pointers.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    141[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 10. No new dependencies. `core`/`std` only. Cargo.toml is already correct — do
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    142[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     not edit it.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    143[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
