[38;5;252m[1m## Two real bugs found by differential testing, not by compiling[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Both were struct-layout errors that a clean build hid completely:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
1. [1m[38;5;10mZSTD_TRACE[0m is 1, not 0.[22m [38;5;10mzstd_trace.h[0m sets it from [38;5;10mZSTD_HAVE_WEAK_SYMBOLS[0m, which is true on GCC/ELF. Sub-agents reasonably assumed the trace hooks were compiled out and dropped the [38;5;10mtraceCtx[0m field from both [38;5;10mZSTD_CCtx[0m and [38;5;10mZSTD_DCtx[0m. The hooks [3mare[23m no-ops (undefined weak symbols), but the fields exist — [38;5;10msizeof(ZSTD_DCtx)[0m came out 95984 instead of 95992, which showed up as a mismatch in [38;5;10mZSTD_sizeof_DCtx[0m and [38;5;10mZSTD_estimateDStreamSize[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
2. [1m[38;5;10msize_of::<ZSTD_CDict>()[0m evaluated to 0.[22m [38;5;10mZSTD_CDict_s[0m was declared as an opaque empty enum for pointer use, so five workspace-sizing expressions in [38;5;10mZSTD_createCDict_advanced2[0m allocated zero bytes for the CDict object. This segfaulted on any [38;5;10mZSTD_createCDict[0m call. I traced it with a [38;5;10mbacktrace()[0m handler, fixed all five sites to use the real layout struct, and then proved by compile-time assertion that the analogous [38;5;10mZSTDMT_CCtx[0m alias resolves to the real struct rather than repeating the mistake.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
